# Every image in this repository comes from the preview panel bundled with the
# package, on invented data: `art/login-*` by `bin/shots.mjs`, `art/panel-*` by
# `bin/panel-shots.mjs` and `art/locale-*` by `bin/locale-shots.mjs`.
# Captures of any real system are ignored on principle —
# they can carry personal or otherwise sensitive data, and a blob pushed to a
# public repository stays reachable by SHA after the file is deleted.
/art/screenshot-*
/art/cover.*
/art/*-shot.*
/art/capture-*

/vendor
/node_modules
# `package-lock.json` and `composer.lock` are both committed on purpose,
# unusual though the latter is for a library. `resources/dist/mia.css` is
# committed too, and CI fails the build when a rebuild does not reproduce it
# byte for byte. That check is only worth running if every input to the build is
# fixed, and there are two: Tailwind, held by `package-lock.json`, and Filament,
# held by `composer.lock` — the stylesheet compiles the framework's core and
# scans its Blade views, so its output moves with the installed version.
# Without both locks an upstream release reports a difference that says nothing
# about the source. Applications installing the package ignore this lock, as
# they do any library's.
.DS_Store
.idea
.phpunit.result.cache
.phpunit.cache
build

# Captures kept for checking rather than for the README. `bin/shots.mjs`
# produces the full set — every composition, both colour modes, both widths,
# with and without a validation error — and only the frames the README uses
# are committed.
/art/verification
# The rejected listing compositions, kept beside the two that shipped as the
# record of what was tried. Same reasoning as `verification`: worth having on
# disk, not worth nine megabytes in a public repository.
/art/listing-candidates
/workbench/storage
